WEBVTT


00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.420
I used to work in private equity,

00:00:01.421 --> 00:00:03.621
so I understand the banking system pretty well.

00:00:03.622 --> 00:00:04.581
And the buy, borrow,

00:00:04.582 --> 00:00:08.101
die method that a lot of people will use that are super rich

00:00:08.102 --> 00:00:10.861
to basically put up their stocks as collateral and keep getting loan

00:00:10.862 --> 00:00:12.361
so they live with the loan money

00:00:12.362 --> 00:00:14.341
is essentially money printing, right?

00:00:14.342 --> 00:00:16.101
Because they don't have to pay taxes on loans.

00:00:16.102 --> 00:00:17.661
So Elon Musk can go say, hey,

00:00:17.662 --> 00:00:20.861
loan me $2 billion and I'll put up my stock as collateral.

00:00:20.862 --> 00:00:22.061
They give him $2 billion,

00:00:22.062 --> 00:00:24.221
and now he doesn't have to pay taxes on that $2 billion.

00:00:24.222 --> 00:00:25.501
He can throw it around willy nilly.

00:00:25.502 --> 00:00:27.961
And the next question people will have is, hey,

00:00:27.962 --> 00:00:29.661
what happens if he doesn't pay the bank back?

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:31.021
The government will bail the bank out.

00:00:31.022 --> 00:00:33.181
Because if you owe the bank $2,000,

00:00:33.182 --> 00:00:36.301
that's your problem. If you owe the bank two billion problems,

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:38.041
that's the bank's problem.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:41.140
And you have to remember that when you have so much money

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:43.981
that you yourself are a market driving factor,

00:00:43.982 --> 00:00:47.021
you have the leverage to create money at will.

00:00:47.022 --> 00:00:48.741
Because if you're borrowing money from the bank

00:00:48.742 --> 00:00:49.941
and all you need is collateral,

00:00:49.942 --> 00:00:53.021
and your stock shares prices can be manipulated.

00:00:53.022 --> 00:00:54.981
You can inflate your stock shares price,

00:00:54.982 --> 00:00:55.941
take out a loan against it,

00:00:55.942 --> 00:00:58.421
and surprise, you now have that super cheap loan.

00:00:58.422 --> 00:01:00.141
And if the bank lends you a bunch of money,

00:01:00.142 --> 00:01:01.501
guess who has to pay it back?

00:01:01.502 --> 00:01:03.501
The government. Because if the bank doesn't,

00:01:03.502 --> 00:01:08.235
they go Under it's truthfully a master class of having unlimited money
